<figure class="pipeline">
  <div class="pipeline-flow" role="img" aria-label="SmashDotNES source-to-player build pipeline: fighter PNG and TOML plus music TOML become generated C and CHR, then smash.nes, then the web player.">
    <div class="pipeline-step"><span>01 · Source</span><strong>Fighter PNG + TOML<br/>Music TOML</strong></div>
    <div class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><code>nessy generate</code><span>→</span></div>
    <div class="pipeline-step"><span>02 · Generate</span><strong>C + CHR</strong></div>
    <div class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><code>cl65</code><span>→</span></div>
    <div class="pipeline-step"><span>03 · Build</span><strong>smash.nes</strong></div>
    <div class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><code>web sync</code><span>→</span></div>
    <div class="pipeline-step"><span>04 · Play</span><strong>Web player</strong></div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Build one ROM. Test it in emulators, then copy that same file to the web player. These checks cover the emulator and browser, not physical hardware or deployment.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
